  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Competition Law and Policy in India</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To support the implementation of the new Competition Law through assistance in the establishment and operation of a well-functioning Competition Commission of India (CCI). The activities to be supported include 1) institutional capacity building of the CCI, 2) training and skills enhancement of CCI, concerned policy makers and supporting legal actors, and 3) an advocacy and outreach program to create greater awareness and support among the key constituencies.  (a) to support the implementation of the Competition Act of 2002 (the Competition Law) through, inter-alia, strengthening the functioning of the Competition Commission of India (CCI), capacity building of CCI staff and other stakeholders; and (b) to strengthen entrepreneurship within the economy and pro-competition allies by promoting greater awareness of the benefits of competition.</narrative>
  </description>
